  ('foundation:ErrorHandler', 'foundation:aiBehaviorRules', NULL, 'An ErrorHandler routes a FlowNode''s exception (unexpected failure) to a designated fallbackNode instead of failing the entire workflow.

How to create:
  assert_individual(class_iri: ''foundation:ErrorHandler'', label: ''...'', properties: [
    {property_iri: ''foundation:appliesTo'',  values: [''<flowNodeIri>'']},
    {property_iri: ''foundation:fallbackNode'', values: [''<fallbackNodeIri>'']},
    {property_iri: ''foundation:hasStatus'', values: [''foundation:Status_1773183515321'']}
  ])

Rules:
- appliesTo must point to a foundation:automation_FlowNode individual
- fallbackNode must point to a node that comes AFTER the failing node in the BFS execution order
- The fallbackNode receives the same ExecutionContext as the failing node (including inputIRIs)
- Only one ErrorHandler per FlowNode is supported — the first one found wins
- ErrorHandlers only activate on exceptions, not on outputIRIs=''failed'' (use a Gateway for that)', 'xsd:string', NULL, 'literal', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 101, 0, 0),
