  ('unit:ARCSEC', 'http://purl.org/dc/terms/description', NULL, '"Arc Second" is a unit of angular measure, also called the $\textit{second of arc}$, equal to $1/60 \; arcminute$. One arcsecond is a very small angle: there are 1,296,000 in a circle. The SI recommends $\textit{double prime}$ ($''''$) as the symbol for the arcsecond. The symbol has become common in astronomy, where very small angles are stated in milliarcseconds ($mas$).', 'qudt:LatexString', NULL, 'literal', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 202, 0, 0),
