  ('unit:AT', 'http://purl.org/dc/terms/description', NULL, 'The $\textit{ampere-turn}$ was the MKS unit of magnetomotive force (MMF), represented by a direct current of one ampere flowing in a single-turn loop in a vacuum. "Turns" refers to the winding number of an electrical conductor comprising an inductor. The ampere-turn was replaced by the SI unit, $ampere$.', 'qudt:LatexString', NULL, 'literal', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 202, 0, 0),
