  ('unit:BIOT', 'foundation:lastUpdatedAt', NULL, '2026-03-04T04:10:29Z', 'xsd:dateTime', NULL, 'literal', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 208, 0, 0),
  ('unit:BIOT', 'http://purl.org/dc/terms/description', NULL, '"Biot" is another name for the abampere (aA), which is the basic electromagnetic unit of electric current in the emu-cgs (centimeter-gram-second) system of units. It is called after a French physicist, astronomer, and mathematician Jean-Baptiste Biot. One abampere is equal to ten amperes in the SI system of units. One abampere is the current, which produces a force of 2 dyne/cm between two infinitively long parallel wires that are 1 cm apart.', 'rdf:HTML', NULL, 'literal', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 202, 0, 0),
