  ('unit:BQ-PER-M3', 'http://purl.org/dc/terms/description', NULL, 'Becquerel Per Cubic Meter ($Bq/m3$) is a unit in the category of Radioactivity concentration. It is also known as becquerels per cubic meter, becquerel per cubic metre, becquerels per cubic metre, becquerel/cubic inch. This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system. Becquerel Per Cubic Meter (Bq/m3) has a dimension of $L{-3}T{-1}$ where $L$ is length, and $T$ is time. It essentially the same as the corresponding standard SI unit $/s\cdot m{3}$.', 'qudt:LatexString', NULL, 'literal', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 202, 0, 0),
