  ('unit:FARAD-PER-M', 'http://purl.org/dc/terms/description', NULL, 'Farad Per Meter ($F/m$) is a unit in the category of Electric permittivity. It is also known as farad/meter. This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system. Farad Per Meter has a dimension of M-1L-3T4I2 where $M$ is mass, $L$ is length, $T$ is time, and $I$ is electric current. This unit is the standard SI unit in this category.', 'qudt:LatexString', NULL, 'literal', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 202, 0, 0),
