  ('unit:L', 'http://purl.org/dc/terms/description', NULL, 'The $litre$ (American spelling: $\textit{liter}$; SI symbol $l$ or $L$) is a non-SI metric system unit of volume equal to $1 \textit{cubic decimetre}$ ($dm^3$), 1,000 cubic centimetres ($cm^3$) or $1/1000 \textit{cubic metre}$. If the lower case "L" is used as the symbol, it is sometimes rendered as a cursive "l" to help distinguish it from the capital "I", although this usage has no official approval by any international bureau.', 'qudt:LatexString', NULL, 'literal', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 202, 0, 0),
