  ('unit:NAT', 'http://purl.org/dc/terms/description', NULL, 'A nat is a logarithmic unit of information or entropy, based on natural logarithms and powers of e, rather than the powers of 2 and base 2 logarithms which define the bit. The nat is the natural unit for information entropy. Physical systems of natural units which normalize Boltzmann''s constant to 1 are effectively measuring thermodynamic entropy in nats.', 'rdf:HTML', NULL, 'literal', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 202, 0, 0),
