  ('unit:ST', 'http://purl.org/dc/terms/description', NULL, '$\textit{Stokes (St)}$ is a unit in the category of Kinematic viscosity. This unit is commonly used in the cgs unit system. Stokes (St) has a dimension of $L^2T^{-1}$ where $L$ is length, and $T$ is time. It can be converted to the corresponding standard SI unit $m^2/s$ by multiplying its value by a factor of 0.0001.', 'qudt:LatexString', NULL, 'literal', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 202, 0, 0),
